Word-list source for the local v0.2.7.1 expansion

Repository: https://github.com/jonathanwelton/word-lists
Revision: 89401c32360e839f36cbe37716e14c5456ce8034
Author named in package.json: Jonathan Welton
Package version: 1.0.0
Files: 3-letter-words.json through 10-letter-words.json

The pinned package.json declares "license": "ISC". The repository contains no
standalone license text. This notice records that declaration without adding
an invented copyright notice or an inferred license grant.

The pinned README attributes the lists to words_dictionary.json from
https://github.com/dwyl/english-words . Its LICENSE.md was inspected at
20f5cc9b3f0ccc8ce45d814c532b7c2031bba31c and is preserved verbatim in
word_lists_origin.LICENSE (Unlicense). This is the observed license of the
named source, not proof of the exact historical revision used by the splitter.

ZhBot merges the 248005 lowercase ASCII entries of lengths 3 through 10 with
its existing seed: 11845 already present, 236160 new, 250871 total allowed
guesses. Existing answer/guess-only roles are retained; new words enter both
the answer and allowed pools. No application code was copied. Source file
SHA-256 / Git blob hashes, counts and the prior seed used for the one-time
database migration are recorded in word_lists_upgrade.json.
